# Pi with a shell, POSIX tools and curl, and no compiler: the README's "Pi with npm",
# whose page installs four device host modules: display, input, download for
# the download tool of Pi's Dolly extension (Janis links its client), and html
# for its ask_user and show_html tools (the html command). The recipe engine
# lets an npm user build an image FROM it (dolly-build).
INSTALL /v0.1.4/Dollyfile-core e68adcf83a11a7fb80b3db20fb1e5676a1cf117c4bd2371128402e06bee15572
INSTALL /v0.1.4/Dollyfile-dollyfile 0410fe5ea027deab03575ae90ed7cf3518b3e7026bd424b9854fbf0870be34e8
INSTALL /v0.1.4/Dollyfile-posix 8687b459b47064010ca3afc8708405c76b6aa2ea2e0a9170e50d277dea8f5b7b
INSTALL /v0.1.4/Dollyfile-display b593af7e2ea91f435014998ebb148e79ef4a3db427d1c8fec35e6978c80545dc
INSTALL /v0.1.4/Dollyfile-curl 8386e296a305c512ea54459d8bd13632449fab9b868c78c9871060afa66b9d81
